rView.swift`\n431\t   - Add \"錄音喚醒語\" row with a navigation link / `.sheet` to `RecordingView(alarm: alarm)`\n432\t   - Show mic icon + \"已錄音\" / \"尚未錄音\" status based on `alarm.recordingName.isEmpty`\n433\t   - Acceptance: tapping the row opens `RecordingView`; saving a recording updates `alarm.recordingName`; saving shows \"已錄音\" status\n434\t\n435\t4. Modify: `SunnyWalker/Views/Home/HomeView.swift`\n436\t   - Gate the \"+\" (add alarm) button and any settings entry behind `ParentalGateView`\n437\t   - Present `ParentalGateView` as a `.sheet`; on success proceed to `AlarmEditorView`\n438\t   - Acceptance: tapping \"+\" presents parental gate before opening AlarmEditorView\n439\t\n440\t5. Add: placeholder `.caf` files to `SunnyWalker/Theme/Sounds/`\n441\t   - Create minimal valid (silent or 1-second tone) `totoro_breath.caf` and `leaf_rustle.caf`\n442\t   - Register them in `project.pbxproj` Copy Bundle Resources phase\n443\t   - Acceptance: `Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"totoro_breath\", withExtension: \"caf\")` returns non-nil; AlarmRingView no longer logs \"no recording — skipping\"\n444\t\n445\t**Carry-overs from today**:\n446\t- `.caf` assets absent → item 5 above\n447\t- AlarmEditorView → RecordingView navigation gap → item 3 above\n448\t- `sampleAlarms` @Model without ModelContext (low priority; do not block Day 6)\n449\t- `AudioPlayer.isPlaying` not auto-reset (low priority; add delegate only if non-loop paths are used in Day 6)\n450\t\n451\t**Constraints**:\n452\t- `ParentalGateView` question must NOT be simple arithmetic — Apple Kids review requirement (§6.4)\n453\t- No third-party SDKs\n454\t- Explicitly list every new `.swift` file in your \"For next (B)\" section — validate.sh [0/4] will catch unregistered files\n455\t- Use theme tokens throughout — zero raw color/font literals\n456\t- Keep 22 tests passing; add at least 2 unit tests for `GateQuestion` logic\n457\t\n458\t**Files to read first**:\n459\t- Spec §4 stage 1 (ParentalGateView full code and `GateQuestion.random()` stub) and §6.4 (App Store compliance / parental gate rules)\n460\t- `SunnyWalker/Views/Settings/AlarmEditorView.swift` (wire RecordingView from here)\n461\t- `SunnyWalker/Views/Home/HomeView.swift` (wire ParentalGate to \"+\" button)\n462\t- `orchestrator/current/ring.md` last 4 entries\n463\t\n464\t→ End of Day 5\n465\t\n466\t\n467\t## [D] Day 6 — 2026-05-31 23:47:00+08:00\n468\tStatus: DONE\n469\tModel:  claude-sonnet-4-6\n470\t\n471\t### Verdict: on_track\n472\tCompletion: 92%\n473\t\n474\tDay 6 brief fully executed: `ParentalGateView` with adult-only questions, placeholder `.caf` assets, `AlarmEditorView → RecordingView` wiring, and HomeView parental gate on \"+\" — all five brief items delivered, 28/28 tests pass, build clean. A also surfaced and wired two previously dormant files (`MarkdownAlarmIO.swift`, `AlarmIOView.swift`) that had been on disk unregistered since an earlier session. The 8% gap comes from three open items: no `UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate` means tapping a fired notification never shows `AlarmRingView` (the app's core clock flow remains unvalidated end-to-end), `AlarmIOView` is accessible without a parental gate (a child can wipe all alarms via the destructive import toggle), and the `.caf` files are silent placeholders that provide no audio feedback on device.\n475\t\n476\t### Alignment with spec\n477\t- ✅ Milestone Day 6 (ParentalGateView §4 stage 1, GateQuestion §6.4 compliance, AlarmEditorView→RecordingView, HomeView \"+\" gated, .caf assets): All five brief items present and complete.\n478\t- ⚠️ Aesthetic / UX: Theme tokens enforced throughout `ParentalGateView` — zero raw literals. Minor: weekday-ordering questions (\"週一 → 週三 → 週五\") and largest-3-digit-number questions (compare hundreds digit) are borderline difficulty for a literate 7-year-old. 3-digit multiplication is unambiguously adult-level. §6.4 compliance holds but the weakest question types are marginal.\n479\t- ✅ On-device only: No new third-party SDKs. `MarkdownAlarmIO` and `AlarmIOView` are pure Foundation/SwiftUI/SwiftData. Zero network calls in any Day 6 file.\n480\t\n481\t### Code quality (spot-checked)\n482\t- `Views/Settings/ParentalGateView.swift`: Clean structure. `WatercolorCard` + `GhibliButton` + `GhibliFonts`/`GhibliColors` throughout — zero raw literals. Shake logic uses `DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter` with seven timed steps — acceptable for a multi-step timed animation sequence (no SwiftUI equivalent). `onSuccess()` called before `dismiss()` — correct. `check()` always assigns a new `question` on wrong answer, so the pool refreshes even before 3 consecutive wrongs; that's fine.\n483\t- `Views/Settings/AlarmEditorView.swift`: `tempAlarm = Alarm(...)` creates a `@Model` without a context; mutations from `RecordingView` propagate via object reference (SwiftData `@Model` is a class). `modelContext.insert(tempAlarm)` in `saveAlarm()` persists the already-mutated instance with UUID stability guaranteed. Functional; non-standard but acceptable for this use case.\n484\t- `Views/Home/HomeView.swift`: `gateDidSucceed` flag + `onDismiss` callback correctly sequences gate sheet → editor sheet without a race. Clean. The IO button (`showingIO`) opens `AlarmIOView` with no parental gate — a child can reach the \"覆蓋現有鬧鐘\" destructive import path. Oversight not flagged in A's handoff stamps.\n485\t- `Services/MarkdownAlarmIO.swift` (first compile today): `timeString` property confirmed present on `Alarm` model. `Alarm` init without `recordingName` defaults correctly to `\"\"`. `parseLine` / `parseRepeat` / `parseTime` logic handles `(off)` suffix, Chinese and English weekday tokens, 24h time validation robustly. No third-party dependencies.\n486\t- `Views/Settings/AlarmIOView.swift` (first compile today): `ShareLink` (iOS 16+), `UIPasteboard`, `TextEditor` — all native. `AlarmScheduler.shared.cancel` called before `modelContext.delete` — correct ordering. Functional.\n487\t\n488\t### Process\n489\t- A: All 5 brief items executed. Went beyond brief by registering and wiring two dormant files — valuable initiative. However the IO button's lack of parental gate was not flagged in A's stamps. 6 new GateQuestion tests added (28 total). Handoff was clear.\n490\t- B: Green verdict accurate. Confirmed all 5 new files (3 Swift + 2 .caf) registered in pbxproj. Clean and concise.\n491\t- C: Correct commit format, accurate daily report, well-targeted tomorrow preview.\n492\t\n493\t### Risks / blockers\n494\t1. **`UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate` missing — CRITICAL**: No delegate is implemented anywhere in the project. Tapping a fired alarm notification opens the app to HomeView with no `AlarmRingView`. The primary child user flow (alarm fires → tap banner → voice dismiss → reward) is broken end-to-end. This has been deferred for 6 days and is now the top blocker.\n495\t2. **`AlarmIOView` not behind ParentalGate**: Child can tap the export/import (↑) button, enable \"覆蓋現有鬧鐘\", paste empty text, and import 0 alarms — deleting all existing alarms. Gate required per §6.4 spirit.\n496\t3. **Silent `.caf` placeholders**: Audio paths execute but produce no sound on device. Notification alarm, AlarmRingView playback, all silent. Blocks audio QA entirely.\n497\t4. **SpeechRecognizer only testable on real device**: `requiresOnDeviceRecognition = true` + zh-TW combination not available in Simulator. End-to-end voice dismissal flow unvalidated.\n498\t5. **Weekday-ordering GateQuestion borderline difficulty**: \"週一 → 週三 → 週五\" may be answerable by a literate 7-year-old who knows weekday names in order. 3-digit multiplication is the only question type that clearly meets Apple's §6.4 bar.\n499\t6. **`sampleAlarms` @Model without ModelContext**: Carried from Day 2. Low priority, no production impact.\n500\t\n501\t### Stamps\n502\t✅ Day 6 brief (all 5 items) fully delivered — ParentalGate, .caf assets, AlarmEditor→Recording wiring, HomeView gate, GateQuestion tests\n503\t✅ 28/28 tests pass — 6 new GateQuestion unit tests all green\n504\t✅ Build clean (rc=0) — `MarkdownAlarmIO.swift` + `AlarmIOView.swift` compile successfully on first registration\n505\t✅ Theme tokens enforced — zero raw literals in Day 6 code\n506\t✅ No third-party SDKs added\n507\t⚠️ `AlarmIOView` accessible without parental gate — child can delete all alarms via destructive import toggle\n508\t⚠️ `.caf` files are silent placeholders — all audio paths produce no sound on device\n509\t⚠️ Weekday-ordering and largest-3-digit-number questions borderline §6.4 difficulty\n510\t❌ `UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate` not implemented — notification tap → AlarmRingView flow is broken; the app cannot function as an alarm clock end-to-end\n511\t\n512\t### For next (A — Coder)  ← TOMORROW's brief\n513\t\n514\t**Primary task**: Implement `UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate` to wire notification tap → `AlarmRingView` — this is the app's single most critical missing path and has been deferred for 6 days.\n515\t\n516\t**Specific work items**:\n517\t1. Modify: `SunnyWalker/SunnyWalkerApp.swift`\n518\t   - Add `@UIApplicationDelegateAdaptor(AppDelegate.self) var appDelegate` (or conform App struct directly via a custom class)\n519\t   - Create `AppDelegate: NSObject, UIApplicationDelegate, UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate`\n520\t   - In `application(_:didFinishLaunchingWithOptions:)`: `UNUserNotificationCenter.current().delegate = self`\n521\t   - Implement `userNotificationCenter(_:didReceive:withCompletionHandler:)`: extract `alarmID` string from `response.notification.request.content.userInfo[\"alarmID\"]`, post `NotificationCenter.default.post(name: .alarmFired, object: alarmID)`\n522\t   - Add `extension Notification.Name { static let alarmFired = Notification.Name(\"SunnyWalkerAlarmFired\") }` in the same file\n523\t   - Acceptance: tapping a fired alarm notification causes `.alarmFired` to be posted with the alarm UUID string as `object`\n524\t\n525\t2. Modify: `SunnyWalker/Views/Home/HomeView.swift`\n526\t   - Add `.onReceive(NotificationCenter.default.publisher(for: .alarmFired)) { note in ... }` to the root view\n527\t   - Match `note.object as? String` → UUID → look up in `alarms` array; store as `@State private var firingAlarm: Alarm?`\n528\t   - Present `AlarmRingView(alarm: firingAlarm)` via `.fullScreenCover(item: $firingAlarm)`\n529\t   - Acceptance: tapping the alarm banner from background/killed state causes `AlarmRingView` to appear with the correct alarm\n530\t\n531\t3. Modify: `SunnyWalker/Views/Home/HomeView.swift` (IO button gate)\n532\t   - Add a second `gateDidSucceedIO` flag (or reuse `gateDidSucceed` with a separate destination enum)\n533\t   - Gate the `showingIO` button behind `ParentalGateView` using the same `onDismiss` pattern as \"+\"\n534\t   - Acceptance: tapping the IO (↑) button first shows parental gate; `AlarmIOView` only opens after correct answer\n535\t\n536\t4. Add: audible `.caf` placeholder assets\n537\t   - Replace silent `totoro_breath.caf` and `leaf_rustle.caf` with a short audible tone (e.g. generate a 1s 440 Hz sine via `afconvert` or use any valid open-license short sound)\n538\t   - Acceptance: `AudioPlayer.play(url: Bundle.main.url(forResource: \"totoro_breath\", withExtension: \"caf\")!)` produces an audible sound; `AlarmRingView` no longer logs \"skipping playback\"\n539\t\n540\t5. Optional: Modify `SunnyWalker/Views/Settings/ParentalGateView.swift`\n541\t   - Replace `largestNumberQuestions` pool with harder alternatives (e.g. calendar month ordering, Roman numeral comparison) that no typical 7-year-old can answer\n542\t   - Acceptance: every question type in the pool would stump a 7-year-old reliably\n543\t\n544\t**Carry-overs from today**:\n545\t- Silent `.caf` assets → item 4 above\n546\t- `AlarmIOView` not gated → item 3 above\n547\t- `tempAlarm` uninserted @Model (monitor; if `recordingName` doesn't persist back, redesign `RecordingView` to accept a `@Binding<String>`)\n548\t- `sampleAlarms` @Model without ModelContext (low priority; do not block Day 7)\n549\t\n550\t**Constraints**:\n551\t- No third-party SDKs\n552\t- Explicitly list every new `.swift` file in \"For next (B)\" section — validate.sh [0/4] will catch unregistered files\n553\t- Use theme tokens throughout — zero raw color/font literals\n554\t- Keep 28 tests passing; add at least 1 test verifying `Notification.Name.alarmFired` is posted when notification is received\n555\t\n556\t**Files to read first**:\n557\t- `SunnyWalker/SunnyWalkerApp.swift` (add AppDelegate + notification delegate)\n558\t- `SunnyWalker/Views/Home/HomeView.swift` (add `.onReceive` + IO gate)\n559\t- Spec §4 stage 3 (AlarmScheduler — `userInfo[\"alarmID\"]` is already set in `content.userInfo`)\n560\t- `orchestrator/current/ring.md` last 4 entries\n561\t\n562\t→ End of Day 6\n563\t\n564\t\n565\t## [D] Day 7 — 2026-06-01 00:35:00+08:00\n566\tStatus: DONE\n567\tModel:  claude-sonnet-4-6\n568\t\n569\t### Verdict: on_track\n570\tCompletion: 93%\n571\t\n572\tDay 7 brief is fully executed: `AppDelegate` + `UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate` are correctly wired, HomeView now handles `.alarmFired` and presents `AlarmRingView` via `.fullScreenCover`, the IO button is gated behind `ParentalGateView`, and audible `.caf` tones replace the silent placeholders. The 7% gap splits across three items: the from-killed-state notification race (A self-flagged; AppDelegate posts `.alarmFired` before SwiftUI's view tree subscribes), two new tests that are technically passing but trivially shallow (they exercise `NotificationCenter` itself, not the delegate code path), and a test-shortcut long-press on TotoroAvatar that bypasses the parental gate and must be removed before App Store submission. Code quality is consistent with prior days — `@MainActor`, theme tokens, zero raw literals, zero third-party SDKs. The `.fullScreenCover(isPresented:)` with manual `Binding` is a minor stylistic concern since `Alarm: Identifiable` makes `.fullScreenCover(item:)` directly applicable and safer.\n573\t\n574\t### Alignment with spec\n575\t- ✅ Milestone Day 7 (UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate, notification tap → AlarmRingView, IO gate, audible .caf assets): All four mandatory items delivered. Spec §4 stage 5 flow `[通知響] → 點 banner → 進前景 → AlarmRingView` now structurally works for the background-suspended path.\n576\t- ✅ Aesthetic / UX: No new UI components — existing theme tokens and patterns unchanged. IO gate uses the same `onDismiss` sequencing pattern as the \"+\" gate; visually and behaviorally consistent.\n577\t- ✅ On-device only: No new third-party SDKs. No network calls. `AppDelegate` uses only `UserNotifications` + `Foundation` frameworks. `.caf` tones are bundle resources, not downloads.\n578\t\n579\t### Code quality (spot-checked)\n580\t- `SunnyWalkerApp.swift`: `AppDelegate` is minimal and correct. `UNUserNotificationCenter.current().delegate = self` in `didFinishLaunchingWithOptions` is the right registration point. `didReceive:withCompletionHandler:` extracts `userInfo[\"alarmID\"]` cleanly, posts `Notification.Name.alarmFired` with the UUID string as `object`, calls `completionHandler()` — all correct. `willPresent:` returns `[.banner, .sound]` — correct for foreground delivery. No issues.\n581\t- `Views/Home/HomeView.swift`: `.onReceive(.alarmFired)` guard chain (string → UUID → array lookup) is safe and correct. `.fullScreenCover(isPresented: Binding(get: { firingAlarm != nil }, set: { if !$0 { firingAlarm = nil } }))` works, but `.fullScreenCover(item: $firingAlarm)` is cleaner since `Alarm: Identifiable` — the `item:` variant passes the non-optional alarm directly to the closure and avoids the manual `Binding` boilerplate. `AlarmRingView(alarm: firingAlarm)` compiles because `AlarmRingView.alarm` is `Alarm? = nil` (set on Day 5). IO gate mirrors \"+\" gate pattern exactly — `showingParentalGateForIO` / `gateDidSucceedIO` / `showingIO` flags sequenced via `onDismiss`. One cosmetic flag: line 42 `.onLongPressGesture { firingAlarm = alarms.first }` is a test shortcut with no parental gate — harmless for QA, must be removed before App Store.\n582\t- `SunnyWalkerTests/SunnyWalkerTests.swift` (`AlarmFiredNotificationTests`): `testAlarmFiredNotificationNameValue` tests a string constant — trivially true, zero production coverage. `testAlarmFiredNotificationIsPosted` posts directly via `NotificationCenter.default` and listens on the same center — it tests the Foundation framework, not any app code. Neither test exercises `AppDelegate.userNotificationCenter(_:didReceive:withCompletionHandler:)`. Day 8 should replace or supplement these with a test that creates an `AppDelegate`, calls `didReceive:` with a mock `UNNotificationResponse`, and asserts `.alarmFired` is posted.\n583\t\n584\t### Process\n585\t- A: Executed all four mandatory brief items, self-flagged the from-killed-state gap and the long-press shortcut before B or C had to catch them. Handoff accurately predicted B's expected validation results. No new Swift files — validated the validate.sh [0/4] check would pass before handing off.\n586\t- B: Green verdict accurate. Confirmed 30/30 tests, build rc=0, .pbxproj check pass. Brief and clean.\n587\t- C: Commit message accurate and well-formatted. Daily report thorough. Correctly surfaced three specific concerns for D (from-killed-state, IO gate race, test depth). No issues.\n588\t\n589\t### Risks / blockers\n590\t1. **From-killed-state notification gap**: When the app is fully killed and the user taps the alarm banner, iOS relaunches the app and calls `AppDelegate.didReceive:` early in the lifecycle — before SwiftUI's scene has built `HomeView` and its `.onReceive` subscription is active. The `.alarmFired` post is dropped silently. Fix: store the pending `alarmID` string in a property on `AppDelegate` during `didReceive:`, then read it in `HomeView.onAppear` and replay the lookup. Medium priority — background-suspended path works; fully-killed state is rare for an alarm app but possible if iOS terminates the app overnight.\n591\t2. **Shallow notification tests**: The two new `AlarmFiredNotificationTests` do not cover the AppDelegate delegate path. If someone removes the `NotificationCenter.default.post(...)` line from `didReceive:`, all 30 tests still pass. This is a false confidence gap.\n592\t3. **Long-press test shortcut in production build**: `TotoroAvatar` long-press → `AlarmRingView(alarm: alarms.first)` has no parental gate. Children can trigger `AlarmRingView` directly. Apple's Kids category reviewer may flag this.\n593\t4. **`.caf` tones are synthetic sine waves**: 440 Hz and 660 Hz tones will wake a child but are not the gentle Ghibli-aesthetic sounds the spec intends. This is acceptable for testing; real audio assets remain an open design task.\n594\t5. **`.fullScreenCover(isPresented:)` vs `item:` binding**: Minor — if `firingAlarm` is set to non-nil, then immediately back to nil before the cover presents (e.g., rapid notification storm), the manual Binding could produce a flash. `item:` binding handles this more robustly.\n595\t6. **`sampleAlarms` @Model without ModelContext**: Carried from Day 2. Low priority.\n596\t\n597\t### Stamps\n598\t✅ `UNUserNotificationCenterDelegate` wired — notification tap → AlarmRingView now works (background-suspended path)\n599\t✅ IO button gated behind ParentalGateView — child cannot access destructive import path\n600\t✅ Audible `.caf` tones in bundle — `AudioPlayer` no longer logs \"skipping playback\"\n601\t✅ Build pass (rc=0); 30/30 tests pass; no new Swift files; .pbxproj check passes\n602\t✅ Zero raw color/font literals; no third-party SDKs; all on-device\n603\t⚠️ From-killed-state path broken — `.alarmFired` post arrives before HomeView's `.onReceive` is registered\n604\t⚠️ `AlarmFiredNotificationTests` shallow — neither test exercises AppDelegate delegate code\n605\t⚠️ Long-press on TotoroAvatar bypasses parental gate — test shortcut must be removed before App Store\n606\t⚠️ `.fullScreenCover(item:)` preferred over manual `Binding` for cleaner semantics\n607\t❌ Nothing newly broken\n608\t\n609\t### For next (A — Coder)  ← TOMORROW's brief\n610\t\n611\t**Primary task**: Fix the from-killed-state notification gap so alarm wakeup is reliable regardless of whether the app was backgrounded or fully terminated; replace shallow notification tests with coverage that actually exercises the AppDelegate delegate path.\n612\t\n613\t**Specific work items**:\n614\t1. Modify: `SunnyWalker/SunnyWalkerApp.swift` (AppDelegate)\n615\t   - Add `var pendingAlarmID: String?` property to `AppDelegate`\n616\t   - In `didReceive:withCompletionHandler:`: set `pendingAlarmID = alarmID` in addition to (not instead of) posting `.alarmFired`\n617\t   - Acceptance: `AppDelegate.pendingAlarmID` holds the UUID string when the notification fires\n618\t\n619\t2. Modify: `SunnyWalker/Views/Home/HomeView.swift`\n620\t   - Add `.onAppear { checkPendingAlarm() }` (or `.task`)\n621\t   - `checkPendingAlarm()`: reads `(UIApplication.shared.delegate as? AppDelegate)?.pendingAlarmID`, clears it, then looks up the alarm and sets `firingAlarm`\n622\t   - Also replace `isPresented: Binding(...)` with `.fullScreenCover(item: $firingAlarm)` — cleaner since `Alarm: Identifiable`\n623\t   - Acceptance: killing the app, firing the alarm notification, and tapping the banner causes `AlarmRingView` to appear with the correct alarm\n624\t\n625\t3. Remove: long-press test shortcut from `TotoroAvatar` in `HomeView.swift` (line 42: `.onLongPressGesture { firingAlarm = alarms.first }`)\n626\t   - Acceptance: TotoroAvatar long-press no longer opens `AlarmRingView` without a parental gate\n627\t\n628\t4. Modify: `SunnyWalkerTests/SunnyWalkerTests.swift`\n629\t   - Replace or supplement `AlarmFiredNotificationTests` with a test that instantiates `AppDelegate`, creates a minimal mock `UNNotificationResponse` (use a real `UNNotificationRequest` with `UNMutableNotificationContent` — no mocking framework needed), calls `didReceive:withCompletionHandler:`, and asserts `.alarmFired` is posted and `pendingAlarmID` is set\n630\t   - Acceptance: if the `NotificationCenter.default.post(...)` line is removed from `didReceive:`, at least one test fails\n631\t\n632\t5. Optional: Replace synthetic `.caf` sine tones with short open-license ambient sounds (forest, birdsong, gentle chime) — the 440/660 Hz tones are functional but jarring for a Ghibli-aesthetic alarm\n633\t   - Acceptance: `AudioPlayer` plays the new sounds without distortion\n634\t\n635\t**Carry-overs from today**:\n636\t- From-killed-state gap → item 1 + 2 above\n637\t- Shallow notification tests → item 4 above\n638\t- Long-press shortcut → item 3 above\n639\t- `sampleAlarms` @Model without ModelContext (low priority; do not block Day 8)\n640\t- `AudioPlayer.isPlaying` not auto-reset for non-loop playback (low priority)\n641\t\n642\t**Constraints**:\n643\t- No third-party SDKs\n644\t- Use theme tokens throughout — zero raw color/font literals\n645\t- Keep 30 tests passing; test count should increase (items 1–4 should net at least +2 meaningful tests)\n646\t- Explicitly list every new `.swift` file in \"For next (B)\" section — validate.sh [0/4] will catch unregistered files\n647\t- `requiresOnDeviceRecognition = true` must remain in `SpeechRecognizer.swift` — never remove\n648\t\n649\t**Files to read first**:\n650\t- `SunnyWalker/SunnyWalkerApp.swift` (AppDelegate — add `pendingAlarmID`)\n651\t- `SunnyWalker/Views/Home/HomeView.swift` (add `.onAppear` check + replace `isPresented:` with `item:`)\n652\t- `orchestrator/current/ring.md` last 4 entries\n653\t\n654\t→ End of Day 7\n655\t\n656\t\n657\t## [D] Day 8 — 2026-06-01 02:08:00+08:00\n658\tStatus: DONE\n659\tModel:  claude-sonnet-4-6\n660\t\n661\t### Verdict: on_track\n662\tCompletion: 96%\n663\t\n664\tDay 8 brief items 1–4 all delivered cleanly: `pendingAlarmID` on `AppDelegate`, `handleAlarmPayload` extracted for testability, `checkPendingAlarm()` on `HomeView.onAppear`, `